# What NOT to upload to EAS Build.
#
# Without this file the project archive was 1.0 GB and the upload died part way
# through with ECONNRESET — 35.6 MB of a gigabyte, over a domestic connection,
# which is a failure mode that looks like a network fault and is really a
# packaging one.
#
# EAS falls back to .gitignore when this file is absent, and .gitignore is the
# wrong list: it is written to keep build output out of GIT, and it keeps
# `android/` out on the grounds that `expo prebuild` regenerates it. But a local
# release build leaves several hundred megabytes of Gradle caches and
# intermediates INSIDE `android/`, and EAS was sweeping those up.
#
# EAS runs `expo prebuild` and `npm install` on its own builders, so none of the
# native output or dependencies below needs to travel.

# Native projects — regenerated by prebuild on the builder.
android/
ios/

# Dependencies — installed on the builder from the lockfile.
node_modules/

# Local build output and caches.
.expo/
.expo-shared/
build/
dist/
web-build/
*.apk
*.aab
*.keystore

# Tests and fixtures. They do not run on the builder and some fixtures are large.
**/__tests__/
**/__snapshots__/
coverage/
.maestro/

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.log
